            <ArticleTitle>Association of multiple sclerosis and intracranial hypertension.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three patients fulfilled the diagnostic criteria for both multiple sclerosis and pseudotumor cerebri. Although coincidence is possible, intracranial hypertension may be a manifestation of demyelinating disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
